      "ts": "2026-03-08T00:17:02.591088-08:00",
      "seq": 28,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Turn 2! I drew another Forest. Opponent played Initiate's Companion (3/1) — aggressive but fragile.\n\
\n\
My plan: Play Forest (untapped), then I have 2 mana (Forest + Thriving Grove). I can cast:\n\
- Skyway Sniper (G) — 1/2 with reach, leaves me 1 mana open\n\
- Elven Bow (G) — equipment, but no creature to equip yet\n\
\n\
Skyway Sniper is better here — it's a body that can block the 3/1 Initiate's Companion if needed (though it would die trading). Actually, the Sniper is 1/2 and the Companion is 3/1. Sniper blocks and dies, killing the Companion. That's a good trade.\n\
\n\
But wait — I should think about whether to play Elven Bow instead. For G, I get an equipment. If I pay 2 more I get a 1/1 token with it attached (making it 2/3 reach). But I only have 2 mana total, so I can't pay the extra 2.\n\
\n\
Better to play Skyway Sniper as a blocker. Let me play Forest first, then Sniper.",
