      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I could also cast Elven Bow for my remaining G mana. But I can't pay the extra 2 for the token. The bow alone is just an equipment sitting there — I'd need 3 mana to equip it later. \n\
\n\
Actually, let me think... If I cast Elven Bow now, next turn I can play a land and have 3 mana. I could cast Llanowar Visionary (2G) or equip the bow to Skyway Sniper (making it 2/4 reach). \n\
\n\
Llanowar Visionary is better on turn 3 — it draws a card and ramps me. I can always play the Bow later. Let me save the mana and not cast Elven Bow now. It's not doing much without a creature to equip.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually casting it now is free since I have the mana and nothing else to do with it. Even if I don't equip it right away, it's on the battlefield ready for when I have spare mana. The opportunity cost is zero since I have 1 untapped Forest and nothing else to cast.\n\
\n\
Let me cast it.",
