      "reasoning": "My turn 3! I drew Silhana Wayfinder (2/1 for 1G, looks at top 4 and puts a creature or land on top). The trade happened — both creatures died.\n\
\n\
Now I need to plan carefully:\n\
- I have 2 untapped lands + 1 land drop = 3 mana this turn\n\
- Options:\n\
  1. Play Forest → cast Llanowar Visionary (2G) — draws a card, gives me a mana dork for next turn\n\
  2. Play Thriving Grove (tapped) → cast Silhana Wayfinder (1G) — 2/1 body + sets up my next draw\n\
  3. Play Forest → cast Silhana Wayfinder (1G) — leaves 1 mana open\n\
\n\
Option 1 is best: Llanowar Visionary draws me a card AND ramps me. Next turn I could have 4 mana (3 lands + Visionary) to cast Ivy Lane Denizen. Then when future green creatures ETB, Ivy Lane Denizen triggers.\n\
\n\
Let me play Forest first, then Llanowar Visionary.",
