      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I took 1 damage (now 19) from the Vampire Envoy. Drew a Forest.\n\
\n\
Now it's my turn 5. I have 4 untapped lands + Llanowar Visionary = 5 mana. With a land drop = 6 mana total.\n\
\n\
My plan: I want to deploy green creatures to trigger Ivy Lane Denizen. Let me think about the best sequence:\n\
\n\
1. Play Forest → 6 mana available\n\
2. Cast Elvish Rejuvenator (2G) → triggers Ivy Lane Denizen (+1/+1 counter somewhere), finds a land\n\
3. Cast Silhana Wayfinder (1G) → triggers Ivy Lane Denizen (+1/+1 counter somewhere), sets up draw\n\
4. That's 5 mana total, leaving 1 mana for Roots of Wisdom? No, Roots costs 1G = 2 mana.\n\
\n\
Actually: Forest + Rejuvenator (3) + Wayfinder (2) = 5 mana. I have 6, so 1 mana left over. Not enough for Roots of Wisdom (2).\n\
\n\
Or: Forest + Rejuvenator (3) + Roots of Wisdom (2) = 5 mana, leaving 1 mana. That mills 3 and gets back an Elf/land.\n\
\n\
Or: Forest + Wayfinder (2) + Roots of Wisdom (2) = 4 mana, leaving 2 mana. Could also cast Band Together (3) but that needs targets.\n\
\n\
I think the best plan is: Play Forest, cast Elvish Rejuvenator (ramp + Ivy Lane trigger), then cast Silhana Wayfinder (card selection + Ivy Lane trigger). Two green creature ETBs = two +1/+1 counters from Ivy Lane Denizen. I can put one counter on Ivy Lane Denizen itself (making it 3/4) and one on Llanowar Visionary (making it 3/3), building a solid board.",
