      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Wait — opponent gained 1 life (19 now) from Vampire Envoy attacking, and they're swinging with it again. The Envoy has flying... but the game is offering me Elvish Rejuvenator and Silhana Wayfinder as blockers. \n\
\n\
Hmm, Silhana Wayfinder is 2/1 — if it blocks a 1/4, Wayfinder takes 1 damage (survives since it has 1 toughness? No, 1 damage kills it since it has 1 toughness). Actually 1 damage to a 2/1 kills it (1 >= 1 toughness). So blocking with Wayfinder trades it for preventing 1 damage.\n\
\n\
Not worth it. Elvish Rejuvenator (1/1) would also die blocking a 1/4. Neither trade is good — I'll just take 1 damage.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — Vampire Envoy has flying. Can these ground creatures even block it? If the game offers them, maybe there's something I'm missing. But regardless, trading a creature to prevent 1 damage isn't worth it.",
