      "ts": "2026-03-08T00:24:44.977375-08:00",
      "seq": 150,
      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "My turn 6! Drew Ghirapur Guide as planned from Silhana Wayfinder. I have 6 untapped lands + Llanowar Visionary = 7 mana. Opponent is tapped out with Canopy Stalker 4/2 (sick) and Vampire Envoy 1/4.\n\
\n\
Let me plan my turn carefully:\n\
- **Ghirapur Guide** (2G = 3 mana): 3/2, triggers Ivy Lane, can make creatures unblockable by power 2 or less\n\
- **Band Together** (2G = 3 mana): Can kill Canopy Stalker before it attacks\n\
- **Roots of Wisdom** (1G = 2 mana): Card draw/selection\n\
\n\
I have 7 mana. I can cast Ghirapur Guide (3) + Band Together (3) = 6 mana, leaving 1. Or Ghirapur Guide (3) + Roots of Wisdom (2) = 5, leaving 2.\n\
\n\
Should I use Band Together to kill Canopy Stalker now? It's a 4/2 that must be blocked — if I don't kill it, it attacks next turn and I must block it (losing a creature). But wait, \"must be blocked if able\" means I'm forced to block, which could trade unfavorably. With Band Together, I can have two creatures deal their power to it. For example, Elvish Rejuvenator (1) + Silhana Wayfinder (2) = 3 power, not enough for 4/2's toughness... I need at least 2 toughness worth of damage. Actually, I need to deal 2 damage total to kill it. So any combination works — even just Elvish Rejuvenator (1) + Silhana Wayfinder (2) = 3, which is more than enough.\n\
\n\
Plan: Cast Ghirapur Guide first (trigger Ivy Lane Denizen, put counter on something useful), then use Band Together to kill Canopy Stalker, then attack.",
