      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Drew Wildheart Invoker! A 4/3 for 4 mana with an 8-mana activated ability to give +5/+5 and trample. The body alone is great, plus it triggers Ivy Lane Denizen. I have 6 lands + Llanowar Visionary = 7 mana.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Wildheart Invoker (2GG = 4 mana), then I'll have 3 mana left for Ghirapur Guide's ability (2G) or Roots of Wisdom (1G).\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think about sequencing:\n\
- Cast Wildheart Invoker (4 mana) → triggers Ivy Lane Denizen → put counter on something\n\
- Then use Ghirapur Guide (2G) to make a creature unblockable by power 2 or less\n\
- Roots of Wisdom (1G) to dig for more cards\n\
\n\
I have 7 mana total. Wildheart Invoker (4) + Ghirapur Guide ability (3) = 7. Perfect.\n\
\n\
But wait, should I cast Roots of Wisdom first? 2 mana to potentially draw a creature. Then cast Wildheart Invoker with the remaining 5 mana. That leaves 1 for... nothing useful. I think Wildheart Invoker + Ghirapur Guide ability is better.\n\
\n\
Let me cast Wildheart Invoker first.",
