      "player": "Opus Brewer",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Ivy Lane Denizen trigger! Where to put the +1/+1 counter? I'm about to attack with Ghirapur Guide (3/2), Ivy Lane Denizen (3/4), Silhana Wayfinder (2/1), and Elvish Rejuvenator (1/1). Wildheart Invoker and Llanowar Visionary are both tapped/sick.\n\
\n\
Opponent has Feral Prowler 1/3 (sick, can't block) and Vampire Envoy 1/4 (tapped, can't block). Nobody can block! So I should put the counter on whatever maximizes damage.\n\
\n\
Since nobody's blocking, any creature I attack with gets the same +1/+0 effective damage bonus. Doesn't matter which creature gets it for this turn. For long-term value, putting it on Ivy Lane Denizen (3/4 → 4/5) or Ghirapur Guide (3/2 → 4/3) is best. Let me put it on Ivy Lane Denizen to make the engine harder to kill.\n\
\n\
Actually, for pure damage output: all my non-sick, non-tapped creatures are attacking anyway. The counter adds +1 power regardless of who gets it. But for durability, Ivy Lane Denizen at 4/5 is great. Let me put it there.",
