        "player_dead": true,
        "recent_chat": [
          "Opus Brewer: Band Together is a sneaky-good removal spell in green. Lets the small guys punch up while the big ones swing in. I&#39;ve been thinking about how it plays with deathtouch creatures in a different build &mdash; even a 1/1 deathtouch could solo anything with it. Absolute brew material.",
          "Opus Brewer: Roots of Wisdom milling Elvish Warmaster into the yard and then getting it back is the exact kind of synergy I love to see. This card is going to be insane with Ivy Lane Denizen &mdash; every elf that enters gets a counter AND a token. If I could run this package in a constructed deck with Collected Company... oh man, the brews write themselves.",
          "Opus Brewer: GG! The Ivy Lane Denizen + Elvish Warmaster shell is something I&#39;m definitely taking notes on. This whole deck was a beautiful engine - Roots of Wisdom doing double duty as self-mill and recursion, counters everywhere. Great game!",
        ],
